## 1. Coordinate frames & conventions (READ FIRST — most bugs live here)

Every motion/vision bug in this codebase traces back to a frame or sign mistake.
Internalize these before editing anything spatial.

- **Heading/angle convention is NON-STANDARD:** `0° = +y = robot forward`,
  `90° = +x = robot right`, increasing **clockwise**. This is *not* the math
  `atan2(y,x)` convention. Almost everywhere the code uses `atan2(x, y)` (note the
  argument order) to honor this.
- **Body frame:** origin at the robot, `+y` forward (out the intake), `+x` right.
  Vision angles/distances and mouse velocity are produced here.
- **Field frame:** origin at field center, axes fixed to the field. LiDAR pose,
  goal constants, and A*/spline planning live here.
- **Body→Field rotation** (used by `ballFieldMm`, `bodyVelToWorld`,
  `bodyToFieldOffsetMm`):
  `[fx;fy] = [c −s; s c]·[bx;by]`, `c=cos(h), s=sin(h)`.
- **Field→Body rotation** (the transpose, used by `fieldToBodyOffsetMm`,
  `fieldVelToBody`, and the Teensy chunk executor):
  `[bx;by] = [c s; −s c]·[fx;fy]`.
  **Invariant:** the Teensy MUST apply the transpose of what the Pi applied. (This
  was a real bug — see C10 in the findings file — now fixed in
  `TrajectoryExecutor::execute`.)
- **Units:** Pi planning/pose is in **mm** and **mm/s**; ball KF internal state is
  **m / m/s**; chunk action velocities on the wire are **m/s**; the Teensy motor
  model works in **rad/s** (wheel) and **volts**. Conversions happen at the
  boundaries — `config::kBallDistToM`, `×1000` in the chunk publisher, `/r_wheel`
  in the executor. Mismatching these is a recurring class of bug (see M1).
- **IMU heading is the absolute authority.** The EKF never estimates θ; it takes
  the Teensy's BNO055 heading as ground truth and only fuses x/y.

