## 2. Hardware & sensors — what each one is and how it is used

| Sensor / actuator | Board | Driver file | How it is used |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Camera** (CSI) | Pi | `camera/CameraCapture.cpp` | libcamera capture → HSV threshold → blob/sector tracking → ball & goal **angles** (and ball distance via pixel calibration). |
| **LD19 LiDAR** | Pi | `lidar/Ld19Reader.cpp`, `LidarDeskewer.cpp`, `LidarLocalizer.cpp` | 230400-baud scan → motion-deskew → wall/line fit → absolute field **(x,y)** pose. Read `docs/LD19.md` before touching. |
| **BNO055 IMU** | Teensy | `CompassSensor.cpp` (on `Wire2`, addr 0x28) | Absolute heading (`getOrientation`, **int degrees**) + yaw rate (`getOmegaRadS`, rad/s, **negated to CW-positive**). Heading is sent to the Pi as the authoritative θ. |
| **Optical-flow "mouse"** | LinePCB → Teensy | `LinePCBComm.cpp` | Body-frame velocity `vx,vy` (m/s). Forwarded to the Pi as telemetry for the EKF dead-reckoning predict step. |
| **Line sensors** | LinePCB → Teensy | `LinePCBComm.cpp`, `LineDetection.cpp` | Field boundary detection → line angle + avoidance angle + chord length + cross-line flag. **Top-priority safety override** in the Teensy loop. |
| **Light gate** | Teensy | `Switches.cpp` | Beam-break ball-in-intake detection → `hasBall` flag in telemetry. |
| **Mode switches + LCD** | Teensy | `Switches.cpp`, `LcdController.cpp` (Serial8) | Start/stop, goal-color selection, role override, calibration triggers. Relayed to the Pi via telemetry (`startEnabled`, `goalIsBlue`, `modeOverride`). |
| **4 drive motors** | Teensy | `Motor.cpp`, `Movement.cpp`, `TrajectoryExecutor.cpp` | Holonomic layout, wheel axes at ≈ ±35° / ±145° from forward (`kWheelAngle*` / `ALPHA_WHEEL`). |
| **Kicker solenoid + dribbler** | Teensy | `Movement.cpp` | `kick()`/`kickBackground()`, `setDribbler()`. (Pi-driven kick/dribble fields are currently padding — see H6.) |

**Inter-board buses (Teensy `main.cpp`):**
- `Serial3` @ 2 Mbaud — **Pi ↔ Teensy** (binary framed protocol; the ONE link that matters for planning).
- `Serial2` @ 1 Mbaud — **LinePCB ↔ Teensy** (line sensors + mouse odometry, `0xA5`-framed binary).
- `Serial8` — **LCD** controller.
- `Wire2` — BNO055 IMU.

