## 8. Communication protocols

### 8a. Pi ↔ Teensy binary framing (the critical link)
Frame: `magic(4) | type(1) | len(2, LE) | payload(len) | CRC32(4)`.
Magic = `0xCEFAEDFE` (Pi `kProtocolMagic`) = bytes `FE ED FA CE` (Teensy
`PKT_MAGIC_BYTES`). Message types:

| Type | Name | Dir | Payload |
|---|---|---|---|
| `0x01` | Ping | Teensy→Pi | `t0` (clock sync) |
| `0x02` | Pong | Pi→Teensy | `t0_echo, t1_pi` |
| `0x03` | ActionChunk | Pi→Teensy | trajectory_id, start_time_pi, dt_ms, num_actions, GlobalAction[] |
| `0x04` | Telemetry | Teensy→Pi | `TeensyTelemetryPayload` (**24 B, `static_assert`'d byte-identical both sides**) |

- **Telemetry** (`TrajectoryExecutor::sendTelemetry` ↔ `Protocol::parseTeensyTelemetry` ↔ `RobotSerial::handleFrame`): heading, mouse vx/vy, omega, hasBall, startEnabled, goalIsBlue, modeOverride, serialLatencyUs. This is how the LCD/switch state reaches the Pi's planner and role arbiter.
- **Clock sync (`ClockSync` / `handleClockPong`):** NTP-style. `latency=(t1−t0)/2`, `clock_offset = t1_pi − t0 − latency`. Chunks are stamped in **Pi time**; the Teensy maps `t_start_teensy = start_time_pi − clock_offset` to schedule execution.
- **Freshness/safety:** chunks are time-indexed; if the index runs past the chunk a **20 ms grace hold** applies, then `emergencyBrake()`. Stale `trajectory_id`s are dropped (note the restart-lockout caveat H4).

### 8b. LinePCB ↔ Teensy (`LinePCBComm`)
`0xA5 | type | len(2) | payload | xor-checksum`. Carries line angle, avoidance
angle, mouse vx/vy, chord length, cross-line flag (`LinePCBDataPkt`, 24 B).

### 8c. Robot ↔ Robot Bluetooth (`team/TeamLink`, `TeamProto`)
RFCOMM link sharing `TeamState` (pose, ball, role claim) at ~30 Hz for team
coordination. Per-robot `kRobotId` / `kPeerBtAddress` must differ (see C6 caveats).

### 8d. Foxglove (debug only — see §11).

---

## 9. Teensy execution (`Offense2026/src/TrajectoryExecutor.cpp`)

`execute()` per loop:
1. Hot-swap the queued chunk when its scheduled start time arrives.
2. Time-index into the active chunk (`elapsed/dt_ms`); grace-hold / brake at the end.
3. Read IMU heading, mouse vx/vy, yaw rate.
4. **Global→body rotation** of the chunk's `vx/vy/ax/ay` using the transpose matrix (§1).
5. **Coriolis feedforward** (`a − ω×v` terms).
6. **Velocity P-loop** (`Kp_x/y/omega`) on the rotation-corrected targets.
7. `executeAsymmetricDrive`: project chassis `(v, a)` onto each wheel, apply the
   motor feedforward `V = kS·soft_sign(ω) + kV·ω + kA·α`, then a **proportional
   voltage safeguard** (scale all four wheels if any exceeds `v_bus`) to preserve
   direction under battery sag. `readBatteryVoltage()` reads the real ADC.

The Teensy `loop()` (`main.cpp`) is now role-agnostic: update sensors → relay LCD
match state → `runRobot()` (drain Pi link, line-avoidance override, execute chunks,
LCD telemetry).

