## 12. Invariants a future editor MUST preserve

1. **Frames must round-trip.** If you change a rotation on one side, change the
   transpose on the other (`bodyToField` ↔ Teensy `field→body`).
2. **Wire structs are contracts.** Any change to `ActionChunk` /
   `TeensyTelemetryPayload` must be mirrored byte-for-byte on both repos and keep
   the `static_assert`. Telemetry has one; the chunk format does **not** yet (see §13).
3. **One reader per UART.** Never add a second consumer of `Serial3` on the Teensy.
4. **The IMU is the only source of θ.** Don't add a competing heading estimate.
5. **The Pi plans; the Teensy executes.** Don't add strategy/planning to the Teensy.
6. **Tunables live in `config.hpp`** (Pi) and the `TrajectoryExecutor`/`Movement`
   constants (Teensy) — keep the motor model numbers in sync (C8).

